### What is the historically accepted definition used to mark the start and end of a "period of military rule" in Nigeria (e.g., coup date, formal inauguration of a military head of state)?
Answer: The historically accepted markers for the start and end of military rule in Nigeria are typically defined by the date of a successful coup (e.g., General Abacha taking power in November 1993) and the formal assumption of office by a civilian president (e.g., Olusegun Obasanjo on May 29, 1999).

