### How many distinct periods of military rule occurred in Nigeria between October 1, 1960, and October 1, 2020?
Answer: Based on the search result, there were two distinct periods of military rule in Nigeria between October 1, 1960, and October 1, 2020. The text states the military dictatorship lasted "from 1966 to 1999 with an interregnum from 1979 to 1983," indicating a break for the Second Republic before military rule resumed in 1983 and ended in 1999.

Source URL: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Military_dictatorship_in_Nigeria

### Using the accepted start and end dates for each military period, what is the cumulative total of days Nigeria was under military rule by October 1, 2020?
Answer: Based on the accepted dates, Nigeria was under military rule for a cumulative total of approximately 10,629 days by October 1, 2020, combining the periods from January 15, 1966 to October 1, 1979 and from December 31, 1983 to May 29, 1999.

Source URL: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Military_dictatorship_in_Nigeria

