The fact-check concludes that President Buhari's claim is **supported** by evidence, as calculations based on documented periods of military rule—from January 15, 1966, to October 1, 1979, and from December 31, 1983, to May 29, 1999—total approximately [10,629 days](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Military_dictatorship_in_Nigeria), which converts to roughly 29.1 years within Nigeria's first [60 years of existence](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Military_dictatorship_in_Nigeria) following its [independence on October 1, 1960](https://www.cambridge.org/core/books/biafran-war-and-postcolonial-humanitarianism/emergences-of-biafra/9BFDE15A5362E7790C78374454594673).